      "kind": "measurement",
      "request": {
        "description": "Measure the compiled MuJoCo arm dynamics, actuator authority, reversal and braking response, and joint-limit reactions without requiring a learned candidate.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "args": [
              "--artifact",
              "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/compiled_dynamics.json"
            ],
            "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/compiled_dynamics.json",
            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "initial compiled dynamics and limit characterization",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.compiled_dynamics"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial decision is whether the likely route to 98% success should first address mechanical reach-and-hold constraints or proceed with policy learning. The physical model leaves effective inertia, actuator realization, and native limit behavior unresolved; these measurements directly discriminate whether poor hold performance would be plausibly caused by weak authority, slow reversals, or limit reactions. High authority and benign limits support a baseline learning route followed by hold diagnostics; low authority, long braking, or active limits redirect the route toward control-aware training and branch selection."
      },
